Our approach leverages our hybrid delivery model, combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement. We have experience in the healthcare domain, including a regional hospital group project, which informs our understanding of the client's needs. Our team includes a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, ensuring a comprehensive approach.

Our proposed solution is based on our Atelier platform, a retrieval-augmented generation platform that can be integrated with existing hospital information systems (SIH) and electronic patient records (DPI). The platform's components include a document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer. We utilize the Sovereign HDS tier on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and EU-only, ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements.

The Atelier platform provides a median latency of 1.3 seconds and common queries have a p95 latency below 2 seconds, meeting the client's response time requirement. We can scale horizontally to ensure high availability, targeting an availability of 99.9%. Our architecture and integration capabilities include API-first design with REST and webhook, allowing for seamless integration with existing SIH and DPI systems.

We support health interoperability standards like HL7 and FHIR through our fhir_hl7_connector, which is in production for main resources and has extended resource coverage on the roadmap. Additionally, we ensure the security and integrity of patient data by adhering to strict data protection policies and utilizing encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant.

Our solution provides drafting assistance for clinical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters, using template-guided drafting. We also provide dossier-handling support by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. The solution facilitates continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, understanding the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and efficient resumption of handling by another professional.

We prioritize data sovereignty, hosting our solution on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and avoiding dependency on non-European suppliers. Our annual operating cost is controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. We propose a cost-optimisation strategy that guarantees the expected quality of service while maintaining a healthy margin.

As part of our sustainable development policy, we aim to reduce energy consumption and rely on low-carbon infrastructure. Our partner, OuraneCloud, uses renewable energy, has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and reuses heat. We practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, minimizing our environmental impact.

Our solution is designed as an assistance tool, with no clinical or medico-administrative decision automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. We ensure explainability of recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution, providing source grounding and audit trails as needed. Our approach is compliant with GDPR, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in healthcare.

We have a comfortable cash runway thanks to our Series A funding of €12,000,000 raised in 2024, and our annual revenue is €6,200,000, which is up around 40% year on year. Our target gross margin range is between 25% and 35%. We propose a phased approach, starting with the framing phase, where we conduct a thorough analysis of the client's requirements and define the project scope.

Our solution meets the client's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool, providing reliable information access, improving care quality, and fitting into existing practices without disrupting workflows. We are committed to delivering a high-quality solution that meets the authority's needs while ensuring data sovereignty, security, and compliance with regulatory requirements.
